        "evidence": "The necessary conditions are: (1) the text labels represent the 'market_share' metric, and (2) the text labels are the authoritative source over the bar geometry. The chart's title 'Browser Usage Share' supports the metric identification. The condition explicitly prioritizes text labels. However, the application of this reading is complicated by the refutation of O2. The reading relies on the set of inscriptions. The actual inscriptions are 38% (Chrome), 44% (Safari), 44% (Edge), 4% (Firefox), and 10% (Others). Under this reading, there is a tie for the highest market share between Safari and Edge (both 44%). The reading does not provide a tie-breaker, and the task requires selecting a single browser. Therefore, while the reading is applicable in principle, it leads to an ambiguous result based on the chart's data.",
